  "boundaries": [
    "This corrects demonstrated full-history copying/serialization cost. The finite old-serializer versus actual delta witness is logical work evidence, not a throughput, latency, allocation or physical write-amplification benchmark.",
    "Normal append syncs the journal, stages/syncs/renames CURRENT, then syncs its parent. The extra small metadata barrier is explicit. Periodic checkpoints retain full logical state and remain history-proportional work.",
    "CURRENT is the sole committed frontier. Every committed frame validates; uncommitted suffixes are ignored read-only and retired only by a subsequent writer. No fallback to older state on committed damage.",
    "Checkpoint restoration reconstructs derived caches before replay. Each replayed delta validates its changed trusted store/cache data. Final restore and weak-subjectivity freshness check precede exposure.",
    "Initial state is staged and published as a whole directory under existing exclusive node ownership. Older bin/json files and incomplete native groups are preserved and rejected; no compatibility migration is provided.",
    "All current anchors and period serving payloads remain. No arbitrary trust-history retention cap or aggregate network/query memory policy is introduced.",
    "Only covered prior generation files are cleaned after durable publication; unknown entries and failed-publication generations may remain. Coherent filesystem rollback and unrelated concurrent local modification are outside integrity guarantees.",
    "No live sync, production dataset, remote host or benchmark campaign. Broader networking/admission, query resources, dashboard, verified offline repair and integrated acceptance remain open."
  ],
